# 🧠 Emily SLM

> A production-quality, GPT-style decoder-only Small Language Model built from scratch in PyTorch.

[![Python 3.12+](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.12+-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/downloads/)
[![PyTorch](https://img.shields.io/badge/PyTorch-2.2+-red.svg)](https://pytorch.org/)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](LICENSE)
[![Code style: black](https://img.shields.io/badge/code%20style-black-000000.svg)](https://github.com/psf/black)

Emily SLM is a research-grade, open-source language model implementation featuring:

- **Custom GPT-style decoder-only transformer** — implemented entirely in PyTorch, zero wrapper around existing models
- **Rotary Position Embeddings (RoPE)** — state-of-the-art positional encoding
- **SwiGLU feed-forward networks** — LLaMA-style gated activations
- **RMSNorm** — efficient pre-normalization
- **Grouped Query Attention (GQA)** — memory-efficient multi-head attention
- **KV Cache** — fast autoregressive inference
- **Flash Attention** — optional hardware-accelerated attention
- **Custom BPE tokenizer** — trained from scratch with tool-calling special tokens
- **Complete training pipeline** — gradient accumulation, mixed precision, checkpointing
- **Full evaluation suite** — perplexity, BLEU, ROUGE, custom benchmarks
- **REST API + Gradio UI** — production-ready serving

---

## 📐 Architecture Overview

```
Input IDs
    │
    ▼
TokenEmbedding ──── (vocab_size → d_model, scaled by √d_model)
    │
    ▼ (if use_rope: no positional embedding added here; RoPE is applied inside attention)
    │
    ▼
TransformerBlock × N
  ├── RMSNorm (pre-norm)
  ├── CausalSelfAttention (MHA or GQA + RoPE + KV Cache + Flash Attention)
  ├── Residual
  ├── RMSNorm (pre-norm)
  ├── SwiGLU FFN
  └── Residual
    │
    ▼
RMSNorm (final)
    │
    ▼
LM Head (d_model → vocab_size, weight-tied to embedding)
    │
    ▼
Logits → Sampling (temperature / top-k / top-p / beam search)
```

---

## 🚀 Quick Start

### Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-org/emily-slm
cd emily-slm
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

### Train a Tiny Model (for testing)

```bash
# Prepare dataset
python scripts/prepare_data.py --input data/raw/corpus.txt --config configs/tiny.yaml

# Train
python scripts/train.py --config configs/tiny.yaml

# Evaluate
python scripts/evaluate.py --model checkpoints/emily-tiny/best --config configs/tiny.yaml

# Chat
emily-chat --model checkpoints/emily-tiny/best
```

### Python API

```python
from slm import EmilySLM, EmilyTokenizer
from slm.config import EmilyConfig

# Load config
config = EmilyConfig.from_yaml("configs/tiny.yaml")

# Build model
model = EmilySLM(config.model)
print(model)  # Shows parameter count and architecture

# Tokenize
tokenizer = EmilyTokenizer.load("checkpoints/emily-tiny/tokenizer.json")
input_ids = tokenizer.encode("Hello, I am Emily!", add_special_tokens=True)

# Generate
import torch
ids = torch.tensor([input_ids])
output_ids = model.generate(ids, max_new_tokens=50, temperature=0.8, top_p=0.9)
print(tokenizer.decode(output_ids[0].tolist()))

# Streaming
for token_id in model.generate(ids, max_new_tokens=100, stream=True):
    print(tokenizer.decode([token_id]), end="", flush=True)
```

### REST API

```bash
uvicorn slm.api.app:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000
```

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/v1/generate \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"prompt": "Hello Emily!", "max_tokens": 100, "temperature": 0.8}'
```

### Gradio Demo

```bash
python slm/frontend/demo.py --model checkpoints/emily-tiny/best
```

